{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3f1d9ddc-3b8a-4311-9e1c-afd610aeb7c2","step":{"id":"s1","script":"We want the area under this line from zero to four. A Riemann sum estimates that area using rectangles.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Riemann sums: rectangle areas"},{"op":"equation","id":"function","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"f(x)=x+1,\\qquad 0\\le x\\le4"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[0,4.4],"y":[0,5.6],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"f(x)"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"curve","y":"x+1","domain":[0,4],"label":"f(x) = x + 1"},{"kind":"segment","from":[4,0],"to":{"on":"curve","x":4},"stroke":"dashed"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"3f1d9ddc-3b8a-4311-9e1c-afd610aeb7c2","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s2"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3f1d9ddc-3b8a-4311-9e1c-afd610aeb7c2","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Split the interval into four equal pieces. Using each left endpoint gives heights one, two, three, and four; each rectangle has width one.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"rectangles","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"polyline","points":[[0,0],[1,0],[1,1],[0,1]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[1,0],[2,0],[2,2],[1,2]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[2,0],[3,0],[3,3],[2,3]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[3,0],[4,0],[4,4],[3,4]],"closed":true,"fill":true}]},{"op":"equation","id":"width","anchor":{"el":"function","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\Delta x=\\frac{4-0}{4}=1"},{"op":"equation","id":"sum","anchor":{"el":"width","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"L_4=\\sum_{i=0}^{3}f(i)\\Delta x=(1+2+3+4)(1)=10"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"3f1d9ddc-3b8a-4311-9e1c-afd610aeb7c2","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The triangles show the missing area: two square units altogether. Our estimate is ten; the exact area is twelve. Narrower rectangles reduce this gap.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"gaps","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"polyline","points":[[0,1],[1,1],[1,2]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[1,2],[2,2],[2,3]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[2,3],[3,3],[3,4]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[3,4],[4,4],[4,5]],"closed":true,"fill":true}]},{"op":"equation","id":"exact","anchor":{"el":"sum","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=L_4+4\\left(\\frac12\\cdot1\\cdot1\\right)=12"},{"op":"text","id":"takeaway","anchor":{"el":"exact","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"More, narrower rectangles → better estimates"}],"checkpoint":null}}
